      ],
      "text": "Role in MS:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " DMTs target the immune system to prevent exacerbations and delay disability; highly efficacious: natalizumab, rituximab, ocrelizumab, ofatumumab, ublituximab, cladribine, alemtuzumab; moderately efficacious: interferon beta 1a/1b, glatiramer, teriflunomide, fumarates, fingolimod and other S1P modulators; growing consensus: high-efficacy tx first line at initiation; if one fails, try another."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Natalizumab:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " monthly infusion; ↓exacerbations and new lesions but may ↑PML risk; PML Sx need an immediate brain MRI (w and w/o gadolinium)."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
